{"schemaVersion":1,"corpusId":"euclid-elements-heath-1908","status":"raw_machine","contentItem":{"id":"euclid-11-2","kind":"proposition","title":"两条相交直线确定一个平面","englishTitle":"If two straight lines cut one another, they are in one plane, and every triangle is in one plane.","book":11,"number":2,"status":"raw_machine","sourceMissing":false,"source":{"urn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:11.prop.2","url":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:11.prop.2/","group":"prop","sourceNumber":2,"corpusSha256":"ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c","hasSourceFigure":true,"historicalChineseUrl":null}},"revision":{"id":"euclid-11-2@raw-3d924e17709dc40c","contentId":"euclid-11-2","version":1,"status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"3d924e17709dc40ca14e713885e409237120ce929bd5f45694f2a13763a727d3","createdBy":"mathforge-corpus-import","changeSummary":"Imported Heath source and machine-assisted Chinese draft. No mathematical or editorial review is implied.","blockIds":["euclid-11-2.statement","euclid-11-2.construction.1","euclid-11-2.construction.2","euclid-11-2.proof.1","euclid-11-2.proof.2","euclid-11-2.proof.3","euclid-11-2.proof.4","euclid-11-2.conclusion","euclid-11-2.source"]},"blocks":[{"id":"euclid-11-2.statement","contentId":"euclid-11-2","revisionId":"euclid-11-2@raw-3d924e17709dc40c","order":0,"kind":"statement","title":"命题陈述","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"92e849a88f7bad814b64f6412f58332c8a11c3c46aa132d50bcdd69541e1e684","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"If two straight lines cut one another, they are in one plane, and every triangle is in one plane."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果两条直线互相切开, 它们就位于平面, 每个三角形都位于平面。"}]},{"id":"euclid-11-2.construction.1","contentId":"euclid-11-2","revisionId":"euclid-11-2@raw-3d924e17709dc40c","order":1,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"986c4b4396ec1f627821e7842dec14a1afd785dda03eac3de08069bff40fd000","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For let the two straight lines AB, CD cut one another at the point E; I say that AB, CD are in one plane, and every triangle is in one plane."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"AB,CD两条直线在E点相互切开;我说,AB,CD在平面线,每个三角在平面线。"}]},{"id":"euclid-11-2.construction.2","contentId":"euclid-11-2","revisionId":"euclid-11-2@raw-3d924e17709dc40c","order":2,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"f3b7144a7f0350856730828bb0586d380a3aa6bbcc1907db8ac4b0af287cfbb9","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For let points F, G be taken at random on EC, EB, let CB, FG be joined, and let FH, GK be drawn across; I say first that the triangle ECB is in one plane."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"F,G点随机地在EC,EB点上,CB,FG点连接,FH,GK点被划过;首先,我说三角ECB是1,平面。"}]},{"id":"euclid-11-2.proof.1","contentId":"euclid-11-2","revisionId":"euclid-11-2@raw-3d924e17709dc40c","order":3,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"45ba2287abca87406e79112ec19f7c1eb16209e589234cac983a01e04073b6af","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For, if part of the triangle ECB, either FHC or GBK, is in the plane of reference, and the rest in another, a part also of one of the straight lines EC, EB will be in the plane of reference, and a part in another."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果三角形ECB的一部分, 或FHC, 或GBK, 属于参考区平面, 其余的则属于另一条, EC, EB 也属于参考区平面, 另一条属于参考区。"}]},{"id":"euclid-11-2.proof.2","contentId":"euclid-11-2","revisionId":"euclid-11-2@raw-3d924e17709dc40c","order":4,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"710fd2645f8f8efb5855404042121dba9dabe73ff2bf2bbea17dd7980017388e","citations":["euclid-11-1"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But, if the part FCBG of the triangle ECB be in the plane of reference, and the rest in another, a part also of both the straight lines EC, EB will be in the plane of reference and a part in another: which was proved absurd. [[XI. 1](/principles/euclid-11-1)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但是,如果三角ECB部分的FCBG部分位于参考文献的平面部分,而其余部分位于另一个部分,那么,两条直线EC、EB部分也将位于参考文献的平面部分,另一部分则将位于参考文献的平面部分:这被证明是荒谬的。 [[XI. 1](/principles/euclid-11-1)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-11-2.proof.3","contentId":"euclid-11-2","revisionId":"euclid-11-2@raw-3d924e17709dc40c","order":5,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 3","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"b0851039d85a3d562629815f8683f514fc75712c366a4ea1e490a8d0985e597e","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore the triangle ECB is in one plane."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此三角形ECB是平面"}]},{"id":"euclid-11-2.proof.4","contentId":"euclid-11-2","revisionId":"euclid-11-2@raw-3d924e17709dc40c","order":6,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 4","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"a679d09d4b926e26869898d66c15069a470e7c1fc3458e73e50e1d29c6478c9d","citations":["euclid-11-1"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But, in whatever plane the triangle ECB is, in that plane also is each of the straight lines EC, EB, and, in whatever plane each of the straight lines EC, EB is, in that plane are AB, CD also. [[XI. 1](/principles/euclid-11-1)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但是,不管三角形ECB是多少,平面也是EC,EB的一条直线,而不论直线平面是多少,EC,EB是多少,平面也是AB,CD。 [[XI. 1](/principles/euclid-11-1)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-11-2.conclusion","contentId":"euclid-11-2","revisionId":"euclid-11-2@raw-3d924e17709dc40c","order":7,"kind":"conclusion","title":"结论","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"823dc261157add573181b25fdf8bd4a416eb067b00e10d19636ebf7b44a07d3e","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore the straight lines AB, CD are in one plane, and every triangle is in one plane. Q. E. D."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,AB,CD直线位于1 平面,每个三角形位于1 平面,Q,E,D。"}]},{"id":"euclid-11-2.source","contentId":"euclid-11-2","revisionId":"euclid-11-2@raw-3d924e17709dc40c","order":8,"kind":"source","title":"来源、译者与开放许可","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"b6b1bf01d7d18520d2ca9af191f096ddd02f69c760c2f504976fe3b375fbcc91","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"provenance","role":"provenance_note","language":"en","status":"generated_metadata","text":"Perseus / Heath source: https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:11.prop.2/\nCorpus URN: urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:11.prop.2\nCorpus SHA-256: ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c\nLicense: CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)"}]}],"outgoingEdges":[{"id":"edge:euclid-11-2:euclid-11-1:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-11-2","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-11-2.proof.2","euclid-11-2.proof.4"],"targetContentId":"euclid-11-1","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:11.prop.2","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:11.prop.2/","sourceLabe